Without separate written permission from the copyright holder, you may not
use the Software or a modified version to operate, publish, distribute, sell,
or otherwise offer a competing app or service to other users.

A competing app or service is one that incorporates the Software and offers
Theama's browser media player, addon integration, media library, or related
features as a substitute for the official Theama app. This includes hosted
web apps, public PWA deployments, downloadable app releases, and services
offered to customers or members. It applies whether access is free, paid,
supported by advertising, or supported by donations.

Changing the name, adding features, or retaining attribution does not remove
this requirement. Publishing source code as allowed by section 2 does not
authorize operating or distributing a competing app. Building and privately
running such a source fork remains allowed by section 2.

This restriction applies to uses of the Software. It does not restrict
independently developed software that does not use protected material from
the Software, or rights you have independently under applicable law.

